  grammar:
  - id: G01-wa
    lesson: 1
    name: "\u306F: the topic"
    pattern: "N1 \u306F N2 \u3067\u3059"
    explanation: "\u306F (read \u308F) marks what you're talking about, and \u3067\u3059
      ends the sentence politely: N1 is N2. \u308F\u305F\u3057\u306F {\u5B66\u751F|\u304C\u304F\u305B\u3044}\u3067\u3059:
      I am a student."
    sheetRow: 2
  - id: G01-neg
    lesson: 1
    name: "\u3058\u3083\u3042\u308A\u307E\u305B\u3093: is not"
    pattern: "N1 \u306F N2 \u3058\u3083\u3042\u308A\u307E\u305B\u3093"
    explanation: "The negative of \u3067\u3059. \u3067\u306F\u3042\u308A\u307E\u305B\u3093
      means the same and sounds a little more formal."
    sheetRow: 3
  - id: G01-ka
    lesson: 1
    name: "\u304B: asking a question"
    pattern: "N1 \u306F N2 \u3067\u3059\u304B"
    explanation: "\u304B at the end turns a sentence into a question. Answer \u306F\u3044\u3001\u301C\u3067\u3059
      or \u3044\u3044\u3048\u3001\u301C\u3058\u3083\u3042\u308A\u307E\u305B\u3093."
    sheetRow: 4
  - id: G01-mo
    lesson: 1
    name: "\u3082: also"
    pattern: "N1 \u3082 N2 \u3067\u3059"
    explanation: "\u3082 means also, and it takes the place of \u306F: \u30EA\u30FC\u3055\u3093\u3082
      {\u5B66\u751F|\u304C\u304F\u305B\u3044}\u3067\u3059, Lee is a student too."
    sheetRow: 5
  - id: G01-no
    lesson: 1
    name: "\u306E: joining two nouns"
    pattern: "N1 \u306E N2"
    explanation: "\u306E joins two nouns, and the first one tells you more about
      the second: \u3055\u304F\u3089{\u5927\u5B66|\u3060\u3044\u304C\u304F}\u306E
      {\u5B66\u751F|\u304C\u304F\u305B\u3044}, a student at Sakura University."
    sheetRow: 6
  - id: G01-who
    lesson: 1
    name: "\u3060\u308C, \u306A\u3093\u3055\u3044: who and how old"
    pattern: "\u3060\u308C\u3067\u3059\u304B / \u306A\u3093\u3055\u3044\u3067\u3059\u304B"
    explanation: "\u3060\u308C asks who and \u306A\u3093\u3055\u3044 asks someone's
      age. \u3069\u306A\u305F and \u304A\u3044\u304F\u3064 are the polite versions.
      Answer with the name or the age, not \u306F\u3044."
    sheetRow: 7
  - id: G01-san
    lesson: 1
    name: "\u3055\u3093: other people's names"
    pattern: "\u301C\u3055\u3093"
    explanation: "Put \u3055\u3093 after other people's names to be polite. Never
      put it after your own name."
    sheetRow: 8
  - id: G01-kara
    lesson: 1
    name: "\u304B\u3089: where you're from"
    pattern: "\u301C\u304B\u3089 {\u6765|\u304D}\u307E\u3057\u305F"
    explanation: "\u304B\u3089 marks where something comes from: \u30BF\u30A4\u304B\u3089
      {\u6765|\u304D}\u307E\u3057\u305F, I'm from Thailand."
    sheetRow: 9
  - id: G02-kore
    lesson: 2
    name: "\u3053\u308C, \u305D\u308C, \u3042\u308C: this and that"
    pattern: "\u3053\u308C / \u305D\u308C / \u3042\u308C \u306F N \u3067\u3059"
    explanation: "\u3053\u308C is near me, \u305D\u308C is near you, and \u3042\u308C
      is far from both of us. If someone asks about \u305D\u308C, answer with \u3053\u308C."
    sheetRow: 10
  - id: G02-kono
    lesson: 2
    name: "\u3053\u306E, \u305D\u306E, \u3042\u306E: this book, that person"
    pattern: "\u3053\u306E / \u305D\u306E / \u3042\u306E + N"
    explanation: "The same three, but they sit right before a noun: \u3053\u306E
      {\u672C|\u307B\u3093}, this book. \u3053\u308C stands on its own."
    sheetRow: 11
  - id: G02-no
    lesson: 2
    name: "\u306E: whose and what about"
    pattern: "\u308F\u305F\u3057\u306E N / \u30B3\u30F3\u30D4\u30E5\u30FC\u30BF\u30FC\u306E
      N"
    explanation: "\u306E shows the owner (\u308F\u305F\u3057\u306E {\u672C|\u307B\u3093},
      my book) or what a thing is about (\u30B3\u30F3\u30D4\u30E5\u30FC\u30BF\u30FC\u306E
      {\u672C|\u307B\u3093}, a computer book). The noun after \u306E can drop: \u308F\u305F\u3057\u306E\u3067\u3059."
    sheetRow: 12
  - id: G02-nan
    lesson: 2
    name: "\u306A\u3093, \u3060\u308C\u306E: what and whose"
    pattern: "\u306A\u3093\u3067\u3059\u304B / \u306A\u3093\u306E N / \u3060\u308C\u306E
      N"
    explanation: "\u306A\u3093 asks what a thing is, \u306A\u3093\u306E asks what
      kind, and \u3060\u308C\u306E asks whose."
    sheetRow: 13
  - id: G02-sou
    lesson: 2
    name: "\u305D\u3046\u3067\u3059: that's right"
    pattern: "\u306F\u3044\u3001\u305D\u3046\u3067\u3059 / \u3044\u3044\u3048\u3001\u3061\u304C\u3044\u307E\u3059"
    explanation: "\u305D\u3046\u3067\u3059 agrees with what was said. \u3044\u3044\u3048
      goes with \u3061\u304C\u3044\u307E\u3059, that's wrong."
    sheetRow: 14
  - id: G02-choice
    lesson: 2
    name: "A \u3067\u3059\u304B\u3001B \u3067\u3059\u304B: either-or"
    pattern: "A \u3067\u3059\u304B\u3001B \u3067\u3059\u304B"
    explanation: "An either-or question puts \u304B after each choice. Answer with
      the choice and \u3067\u3059, not \u306F\u3044 or \u3044\u3044\u3048."
    sheetRow: 15
  - id: G03-koko
    lesson: 3
    name: "\u3053\u3053, \u305D\u3053, \u3042\u305D\u3053: places"
    pattern: "\u3053\u3053 / \u305D\u3053 / \u3042\u305D\u3053 \u306F N \u3067\u3059"
    explanation: "Places: here, there by you, and over there. \u3053\u3061\u3089,
      \u305D\u3061\u3089 and \u3042\u3061\u3089 are the polite versions."
    sheetRow: 16
  - id: G03-doko
    lesson: 3
    name: "\u3069\u3053, \u3069\u3061\u3089: where"
    pattern: "N \u306F \u3069\u3053\u3067\u3059\u304B"
    explanation: "\u3069\u3053 asks where, and \u3069\u3061\u3089 is the polite version.
      \u304A{\u56FD|\u304F\u306B}\u306F \u3069\u3061\u3089\u3067\u3059\u304B asks
      which country someone is from. Use \u306F before \u3069\u3053\u3067\u3059\u304B."
    sheetRow: 17
  - id: G03-no
    lesson: 3
    name: "\u306E: made in"
    pattern: "{\u65E5\u672C|\u306B\u307B\u3093}\u306E N"
    explanation: "\u306E can show where a thing is from or made: {\u65E5\u672C|\u306B\u307B\u3093}\u306E
      \u304F\u308B\u307E, a Japanese car. \u3069\u3053\u306E asks where it's from."
    sheetRow: 18
  - id: G03-ikura
    lesson: 3
    name: "\u3044\u304F\u3089: how much"
    pattern: "N \u306F \u3044\u304F\u3089\u3067\u3059\u304B"
    explanation: "\u3044\u304F\u3089 asks the price. Answer with the amount and {\u5186|\u3048\u3093}:
      500{\u5186|\u3048\u3093}\u3067\u3059."
    sheetRow: 19
  - id: G03-count
    lesson: 3
    name: Numbers that change sound
    pattern: "\u3055\u3093\u3073\u3083\u304F / \u306F\u3063\u305B\u3093 / \u3055\u3093\u304C\u3044"
    explanation: "Some numbers change sound when they join: 300 is \u3055\u3093\u3073\u3083\u304F,
      8,000 is \u306F\u3063\u305B\u3093, the 3rd floor is \u3055\u3093\u304C\u3044.
      \u306A\u3093\u304C\u3044 asks which floor."
    sheetRow: 20
  - id: G04-time
    lesson: 4
    name: "\u301C\u3058\u301C\u3075\u3093: telling the time"
    pattern: "{\u4ECA|\u3044\u307E} \u301C{\u6642|\u3058}\u301C{\u5206|\u3075\u3093}\u3067\u3059"
    explanation: "\u306A\u3093\u3058 asks the time. Watch the readings: 4{\u6642|\u3058}
      \u3088\u3058, 7{\u6642|\u3058} \u3057\u3061\u3058, 9{\u6642|\u3058} \u304F\u3058,
      10{\u5206|\u3077\u3093} \u3058\u3085\u3063\u3077\u3093. {\u5348\u524D|\u3054\u305C\u3093}
      is a.m. and {\u5348\u5F8C|\u3054\u3054} is p.m."
    sheetRow: 21
  - id: G04-masu
    lesson: 4
    name: "\u307E\u3059 forms: do, don't, did, didn't"
    pattern: "\u301C\u307E\u3059 / \u301C\u307E\u305B\u3093 / \u301C\u307E\u3057\u305F
      / \u301C\u307E\u305B\u3093\u3067\u3057\u305F"
    explanation: Polite verbs change their ending for the negative and the past.
      A past question needs a past answer.
    sheetRow: 22
  - id: G04-ni
    lesson: 4
    name: "\u306B: at a time"
    pattern: "\u301C{\u6642|\u3058}\u306B V"
    explanation: "\u306B marks the time something happens: 6{\u6642|\u3058}\u306B
      {\u8D77|\u304A}\u304D\u307E\u3059, I get up at 6."
    sheetRow: 23
  - id: G04-kara
    lesson: 4
    name: "\u304B\u3089, \u307E\u3067: from and until"
    pattern: "\u301C\u304B\u3089 \u301C\u307E\u3067"
    explanation: "\u304B\u3089 marks the start and \u307E\u3067 marks the end: 9{\u6642|\u3058}\u304B\u3089
      5{\u6642|\u3058}\u307E\u3067, from 9 until 5."
    sheetRow: 24
  - id: G04-to
    lesson: 4
    name: "\u3068: and"
    pattern: "N \u3068 N"
    explanation: "\u3068 joins nouns: {\u571F\u66DC\u65E5|\u3069\u3088\u3046\u3073}\u3068
      {\u65E5\u66DC\u65E5|\u306B\u3061\u3088\u3046\u3073}, Saturday and Sunday."
    sheetRow: 25
  - id: G04-ne
    lesson: 4
    name: "\u306D: sharing a feeling"
    pattern: "\u301C\u306D"
    explanation: "\u306D at the end shares a feeling and invites the listener to
      agree."
    sheetRow: 26
  - id: G05-he
    lesson: 5
    name: "\u3078: going somewhere"
    pattern: "{\u5834\u6240|\u3070\u3057\u3087}\u3078 {\u884C|\u3044}\u304D\u307E\u3059"
    explanation: "\u3078 (read \u3048) marks where you're heading with {\u884C|\u3044}\u304D\u307E\u3059,
      {\u6765|\u304D}\u307E\u3059 and {\u5E30|\u304B\u3048}\u308A\u307E\u3059. \u306B
      works too."
    sheetRow: 27
  - id: G05-de
    lesson: 5
    name: "\u3067: by train, by bus"
    pattern: "{\u96FB\u8ECA|\u3067\u3093\u3057\u3083}\u3067 {\u884C|\u3044}\u304D\u307E\u3059"
    explanation: "\u3067 marks how you travel. \u306A\u3093\u3067 asks how. On foot
      is {\u6B69|\u3042\u308B}\u3044\u3066, with no \u3067."
    sheetRow: 28
  - id: G05-to
    lesson: 5
    name: "\u3068: with someone"
    pattern: "{\u53CB\u9054|\u3068\u3082\u3060\u3061}\u3068 {\u884C|\u3044}\u304D\u307E\u3059"
    explanation: "\u3068 marks who you do something with, and \u3060\u308C\u3068
      asks who with. {\u4E00\u4EBA|\u3072\u3068\u308A}\u3067 means alone."
    sheetRow: 29
  - id: G05-itsu
    lesson: 5
    name: "\u3044\u3064 and dates"
    pattern: "\u3044\u3064 / \u301C{\u6708|\u304C\u3064}\u301C{\u65E5|\u306B\u3061}"
    explanation: "\u3044\u3064 asks when. Some dates have their own readings: the
      1st is \u3064\u3044\u305F\u3061, the 8th is \u3088\u3046\u304B, and April is
      \u3057\u304C\u3064."
    sheetRow: 30
  - id: G05-nimo
    lesson: 5
    name: "\u3069\u3053\u3082 + negative: nowhere"
    pattern: "\u3069\u3053(\u3078)\u3082 {\u884C|\u3044}\u304D\u307E\u305B\u3093"
    explanation: "A question word with \u3082 and a negative verb means not anywhere,
      or nothing at all."
    sheetRow: 31
  - id: G05-yo
    lesson: 5
    name: "\u3088: telling someone"
    pattern: "\u301C\u3088"
    explanation: "\u3088 at the end tells the listener something they don't know
      yet."
    sheetRow: 32
  - id: G06-wo
    lesson: 6
    name: "\u3092: the thing you act on"
    pattern: "N \u3092 V"
    explanation: "\u3092 marks the thing an action is done to: \u30D1\u30F3\u3092
      {\u98DF|\u305F}\u3079\u307E\u3059, I eat bread. Sports and activities take
      \u3092 with \u3057\u307E\u3059."
    sheetRow: 33
  - id: G06-de
    lesson: 6
    name: "\u3067: where it happens"
    pattern: "{\u5834\u6240|\u3070\u3057\u3087}\u3067 V"
    explanation: "\u3067 marks the place where an action happens: {\u56F3\u66F8\u9928|\u3068\u3057\u3087\u304B\u3093}\u3067
      {\u52C9\u5F37|\u3079\u3093\u304D\u3087\u3046}\u3057\u307E\u3059. \u3078 is
      where you go, \u3067 is where you do it."
    sheetRow: 34
  - id: G06-nani
    lesson: 6
    name: "\u306A\u306B\u3092: what will you do"
    pattern: "{\u4F55|\u306A\u306B}\u3092 \u3057\u307E\u3059\u304B"
    explanation: "\u306A\u306B\u3092 asks what you'll do or what thing. Answer with
      the thing and \u3092."
    sheetRow: 35
  - id: G06-ni
    lesson: 6
    name: "\u306B: meeting someone"
    pattern: "N \u306B {\u4F1A|\u3042}\u3044\u307E\u3059"
    explanation: "{\u4F1A|\u3042}\u3044\u307E\u3059 takes \u306B (or \u3068) for
      the person you meet."
    sheetRow: 36
  - id: G06-invite
    lesson: 6
    name: "\u307E\u305B\u3093\u304B, \u307E\u3057\u3087\u3046: inviting"
    pattern: "\u3044\u3063\u3057\u3087\u306B \u301C\u307E\u305B\u3093\u304B"
    explanation: "\u307E\u305B\u3093\u304B invites someone politely: won't you...?
      \u307E\u3057\u3087\u3046 means let's. Say yes with \u3048\u3048\u3001\u301C\u307E\u3057\u3087\u3046."
    sheetRow: 37
  - id: G06-souka
    lesson: 6
    name: "\u305D\u3046\u3067\u3059\u304B: oh, I see"
    pattern: "\u305D\u3046\u3067\u3059\u304B"
    explanation: "With a falling tone, \u305D\u3046\u3067\u3059\u304B means oh, I
      see. It shows you heard something new."
    sheetRow: 38
